# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SECURITY HEADERS — served by Cloudflare Workers Assets
#
#  wrangler.jsonc binds `.open-next/assets` as ASSETS, and Cloudflare serves a
#  matching static file DIRECTLY from that layer without ever invoking the
#  Worker. THIS FILE IS WHAT COVERS THOSE RESPONSES. next.config.ts parses it
#  so the Worker sends the same set — with one exception it enforces there:
#  the Content-Security-Policy is NOT lifted.
#
#  The reason is that OpenNext keeps no HTML here (`find .open-next/assets
#  -name '*.html'` comes back empty): every document is rendered by the
#  Worker, where middleware.ts answers it with a per-request nonce. Sending
#  this policy as well only added a second one — Cloudflare comma-joins them
#  and the browser enforces the intersection, which is how the homepage video
#  came to be blocked by a policy that explicitly allows YouTube. So the
#  policy below governs scripts, styles, fonts and images served from the
#  asset layer; middleware.ts governs documents. Keep a directive a document
#  needs in BOTH, or it will not be in effect where it matters.
#
#  script-src is deliberately `'self'` with no `'unsafe-inline'`: nothing the
#  asset layer serves is a document, so nothing here needs an inline
#  allowance, and a policy that grants one anyway is read as the site's
#  script policy by anyone scanning it.
#
#  connect-src script.google.com — the waitlist and Book-a-demo forms POST to
#  the Apps Script lead endpoint (lib/sheet-sync.ts). The googleusercontent
#  origin is the redirect target of that POST, and connect-src is enforced
#  against redirects too.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), browsing-topics=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://i.ytimg.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://script.google.com https://script.googleusercontent.com; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; upgrade-insecure-requests
